input_precision='ieee' (true fp32 dot) which on A800 is ~3-4x slower than bf16 HMMA and does NOT use the fast tensor-core path; (b) c007==c009 proved matmul precision is IRRELEVANT to the compared result for these workloads, so bf16 HMMA will still pass 5/5. Reverting the GEMM to bf16 is the single biggest, zero-correctness-risk speed lever. c011 = c010 with the GEMM reverted to bf16 (drop .to(fp32) upcast and input_precision='ieee'; keep everything else). Expect a large speedup toward/above 1.0x.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 10, \"skills_used\": \"none\", \"next_candidate_plan\": \"c011 (parent c010): revert gate GEMM to bf16 HMMA (remove the fp32 tile upcast and input_precision='ieee'; acc += tl.dot(a_bf16, b_bf16)), keeping c010's exact routing + torch.topk output order. Single-variable perf change; precision proven comparison-irrelevant (c007==c009). Then tile/tune GEMM (BLOCK_M/BLOCK_K/num_stages>=2/num_warps) and consider re-fusing the two kernels to cut the logits DRAM round-trip + second launch.\"}","originalFile":"{\"candidate\": \"c001\", \"parent\": null, \"source_sha256\": \"52c4f1c15f562cd519e56e01dc682e982d8118679fe58a6f6c2c46225c06cb8a\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T00:00:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Fused bf16-HMMA fp32-accum gate GEMM + fp32 iterative-argmax routing epilogue (3D-reshape group stage, 3D broadcast mask expansion) passes all 5 feedback workloads and beats the multi-launch reference.\", \"config\": {\"BLOCK_M\": 32, \"BLOCK_K\": 64, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 3, \"matmul_precision\": \"bf16\", \"epilogue\": \"3D reshape group top-2, tl.trans(w) GEMM, dot(acc-arg), python-list companion capture\"}, \"validation\": {\"static_gate_passed\": true, \"static_gate_notes\": \"two score arrays; bias selection-only; fp32 epilogue; -inf sentinel; int64/fp32 outputs; tail m_mask\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"469b2796-deb3-5a83-a7a6-1b2f84b86f20\", \"num_tokens\": 2240, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"993dd417-9fb2-5d66-9b81-c1e15a113463\", \"num_tokens\": 2272, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"0fc8f5f9-1900-55f4-b7d8-acefecbead69\", \"num_tokens\": 6144, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"d6d0eb83-de2e-5a6d-ba23-ee72ae216708\", \"num_tokens\": 2048, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"1d554a6c-1d9d-54c7-9ed9-6d4b50c95906\", \"num_tokens\": 2112, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"all_correct\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"decision\": \"discard\", \"decision_reason\": \"0/5 RUNTIME_ERROR on all workloads; evaluator exposes no Python traceback. Highest-risk constructs are the 3D reshape + axis-2 reductions in the group stage and the 3D broadcast_to mask expansion (Triton 3D reduce/broadcast is the flakiest surface on this stack), plus register pressure from several concurrent [32,256] fp32 tensors. Next candidate keeps identical numerics but replaces all 3D ops with 2D static-unroll over the 8 groups, loads weight pre-transposed to drop tl.trans, and lowers BLOCK_M to relieve pressure.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 1, \"skills_used\": \"none\", \"next_candidate_plan\": \"c002: fully 2D epilogue (static-unroll 8 groups, no 3D reshape/broadcast), pre-transposed weight load, BLOCK_M=16\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c002\", \"parent\": \"c001\", \"source_sha256\": \"b42de18dda7f9b54b7a54ec8f3e83e11f8df02791d7164b2fb6d04de3de6dab0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:24:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"c001's 0/5 RUNTIME_ERROR was caused by the 3D reshape + axis-2 group reductions and the 3D broadcast_to mask expansion; replacing the epilogue with a fully-2D static-unroll over the 8 groups (masked 2D reductions over the 256-wide expert axis, 2D (offs_e//EPG)==gi mask, pre-transposed weight to drop tl.trans, BLOCK_M=16) keeps identical numerics and compiles/runs on this Triton stack.\", \"config\": {\"BLOCK_M\": 16, \"BLOCK_K\": 64, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 3, \"matmul_precision\": \"bf16\", \"epilogue\": \"fully-2D static-unroll 8 groups (no 3D reshape/broadcast), pre-transposed weight load (no tl.trans), 3-arg tl.dot(hs,w,acc), tl.argmax selection, int64 store, python-list companion capture\"}, \"validation\": {\"static_gate_passed\": true, \"static_gate_notes\": \"two score arrays; bias selection-only; fp32 epilogue; top-2 sum per group; 4 groups; -inf sentinel; top-8 experts; bias-free companion via masked sum; +1e-20 then *scaling; int64/fp32 outputs; tail m_mask; all epilogue 2D\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"469b2796-deb3-5a83-a7a6-1b2f84b86f20\", \"num_tokens\": 2240, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"993dd417-9fb2-5d66-9b81-c1e15a113463\", \"num_tokens\": 2272, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"0fc8f5f9-1900-55f4-b7d8-acefecbead69\", \"num_tokens\": 6144, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"d6d0eb83-de2e-5a6d-ba23-ee72ae216708\", \"num_tokens\": 2048, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"1d554a6c-1d9d-54c7-9ed9-6d4b50c95906\", \"num_tokens\": 2112, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"all_correct\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"decision\": \"discard\", \"decision_reason\": \"0/5 RUNTIME_ERROR again, identical to c001 despite a structurally very different (fully-2D) epilogue. This RULES OUT the 3D reshape/broadcast and tl.trans as the fault: the failing construct is COMMON to c001 and c002. Remaining shared suspects, none observable via traceback (evaluator exposes only RUNTIME_ERROR): (a) 3-arg tl.dot(hs,w,acc) [older Triton reads arg3 as trans_a -> type error], (b) tl.argmax(axis=1), (c) int64 tl.store from kernel, (d) tl.sigmoid on a [BLOCK_M,256] tile. Next candidate c003 removes (a),(b),(c) at