lapse to <=atol -> ordering was the issue (tune/ done). If indices still mismatch hugely -> try descending-by-score canonicalization; if only small weight diffs remain -> precision escalation.\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c008\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_sha256\": \"24b37ce57503b51b6c9f97ac62cffebedfc88e914879511a70f73dae0fed23fe\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T23:51:10Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"c007's positional topk_idx mismatch was pure output ORDER: the reference torch.topk(sorted=False) returns experts in ASCENDING EXPERT INDEX, not descending-by-score. Reordering the 8 selected (idx,weight) pairs to ascending expert index (rank[i]=sum_j(sel_idx[j]<sel_idx[i]), scatter store) while keeping c007's proven-runnable kernel and selected SET/weights unchanged should collapse the error under tolerance.\", \"config\": {\"arch\": \"two-kernel split\", \"gemm\": {\"BLOCK_M\": 16, \"BLOCK_K\": 32, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1, \"precision\": \"bf16\"}, \"route\": {\"grid\": \"(T,)\", \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1}, \"output_order\": \"ascending expert index (8x8 rank + scatter store)\", \"sigmoid\": \"1/(1+exp(-x))\", \"sentinel\": \"-1e30\"}, \"validation\": {\"static_gate_passed\": true, \"static_gate_notes\": \"identical to c007 except output pairs scatter-stored to slot rank[i]=#{j: sel_idx[j]<sel_idx[i]}; selected experts distinct so rank is a permutation of 0..7; set and weight values unchanged\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"469b2796-deb3-5a83-a7a6-1b2f84b86f20\", \"num_tokens\": 2240, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"max_abs\": 249.0, \"max_rel\": 49.8}, {\"uuid\": \"993dd417-9fb2-5d66-9b81-c1e15a113463\", \"num_tokens\": 2272, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"max_abs\": 241.0, \"max_rel\": 48.2}, {\"uuid\": \"0fc8f5f9-1900-55f4-b7d8-acefecbead69\", \"num_tokens\": 6144, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"max_abs\": 235.0, \"max_rel\": 29.375}, {\"uuid\": \"d6d0eb83-de2e-5a6d-ba23-ee72ae216708\", \"num_tokens\": 2048, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"max_abs\": 181.0, \"max_rel\": 4.31}, {\"uuid\": \"1d554a6c-1d9d-54c7-9ed9-6d4b50c95906\", \"num_tokens\": 2112, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"max_abs\": 238.0, \"max_rel\": 119.0}], \"all_correct\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"decision\": \"discard\", \"decision_reason\": \"Still INCORRECT_NUMERICAL, max_abs (181-249) essentially unchanged vs c007 (190-249) and still in the expert-index range [0,255]. Two DIFFERENT output orders (c007 descending-by-score, c008 ascending-index) both fail with ~identical index-magnitude errors. If only the ORDER were wrong, at least one of these two natural orders would have matched; since NEITHER does, the selected SET itself must differ from the reference on enough rows to break the >=0.99 match ratio. The one factor common to c007 and c008 that perturbs selection is the bf16 gate GEMM: the reference computes logits via F.linear(hidden.float(), weight.float()) = a TRUE fp32 matmul over the bf16 inputs upcast to fp32, whereas c007/c008 multiply in bf16 tensor cores. bf16 rounding shifts borderline sigmoid+bias values, flipping which group is 4th and which expert is 8th on a fraction of tokens -> wrong selected set -> positional index blowup regardless of order. Fix = make the GEMM numerically faithful. c009 (parent c007, single-variable change: GEMM precision only) upcasts the bf16 tiles to fp32 and uses tl.dot(input_precision='ieee') for a real fp32 accumulate matching the reference exactly, and restores c007's descending-by-score emit (torch.topk on CUDA returns descending). If c009 passes -> exact fp32 GEMM was the fix. If c009 still mismatches indices -> the reference order is not descending; c010 keeps exact GEMM + ascending-index emit to separate order from set.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 8, \"skills_used\": \"none\", \"next_candidate_plan\": \"c009 (parent c007): exact fp32 gate GEMM -- load bf16 tiles, .to(fp32), tl.dot(input_precision='ieee') true-fp32 accumulate (matches reference F.linear(.float())); restore c007 descending-by-score output order; single-variable change vs c007 (precision only). Then, once correct, trade precision back for speed (tf32x3/bf16) watching the 0.99 match ratio, and re-fuse / tile-tune for geomean.\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c009\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_sha256\": \"02657b0ad88d17f9add49ade3d5aef557b60e3c51e7c855b9845e22d018540f9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T00:28:10Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"The wrong selected SET in c007/c008 came from the bf16 gate GEMM diverging from the reference's fp32 F.linear; an exact fp32 GEMM (upcast bf16 tiles to fp32, tl.dot(input_precision='ieee') true-fp32 accumulate) with c007's descending-by-score emit will match the reference set+order and pass.\", \"config\": {\"arch\": \"two-kernel split\", \"gemm\": {\"BLOCK_M\": 16, \"BLOCK_K\": 32, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1, \"precision\": \"ieee (fp32 upcast tiles, true fp32 accumulate)\"}, \"route\": {\"grid\": \"(T,)\", \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1}, \"output_order\": \"descending by masked (sigmoid+bias) score\", \"sigmoid\": \"1/(1+exp(-x))\", \"sentinel\": \"-1e30\"}, \"validation\": {\"static_gate_passed\": true, \"static_gate_notes\": \"identical to c007 except GEMM upcasts tiles to fp32 and uses input_precision='ieee'; with exact fp32 logits my group top-2 sum, top-4 groups, mask, and top-8 experts are provably the SAME SET as the reference (all fp32 deterministic); descending emit\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"469b2796-deb3-5a83-a7a6-1b2f84b86f20\", \"num_tokens\": 2240, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"max_abs\": 249.0, \"max_rel\": 49.8}, {\"uuid\": \"993dd417-9fb2-5d66-9b81-c1e15a113463\", \"num_tokens\": 2272, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup