ference order. Since c007 (descending by masked sigmoid+bias, identical key to the reference's masked_scores) does NOT match, the reference is NOT in descending-score order; the most likely captured order from torch.topk(sorted=False) on CUDA is ASCENDING EXPERT INDEX. c008 reorders the 8 selected (idx,weight) pairs by ascending expert index via an 8x8 rank (sum of sel_idx[j]<sel_idx[i]) + scatter store, keeping the now-proven-runnable kernel structure otherwise identical.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 7, \"skills_used\": \"none\", \"next_candidate_plan\": \"c008: keep c007's runnable two-kernel structure; reorder the top-8 outputs to ASCENDING EXPERT INDEX before storing -- compute rank[i]=sum_j(sel_idx[j]<sel_idx[i]) over the 8 selected (tiny 8x8), then scatter-store sel_idx and w_vec to slot rank[i]. If errors collapse to <=atol -> ordering was the issue (tune/ done). If indices still mismatch hugely -> try descending-by-score canonicalization; if only small weight diffs remain -> precision escalation.\"}"," {\"candidate\": \"c008\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_sha256\": \"24b37ce57503b51b6c9f97ac62cffebedfc88e914879511a70f73dae0fed23fe\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T23:51:10Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"c007's positional topk_idx mismatch was pure output ORDER: the reference torch.topk(sorted=False) returns experts in ASCENDING EXPERT INDEX, not descending-by-score. Reordering the 8 selected (idx,weight) pairs to ascending expert index (rank[i]=sum_j(sel_idx[j]<sel_idx[i]), scatter store) while keeping c007's proven-runnable kernel and selected SET/weights unchanged should collapse the error under tolerance.\", \"config\": {\"arch\": \"two-kernel split\", \"gemm\": {\"BLOCK_M\": 16, \"BLOCK_K\": 32, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1, \"precision\": \"bf16\"}, \"route\": {\"grid\": \"(T,)\", \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1}, \"output_order\": \"ascending expert index (8x8 rank + scatter store)\", \"sigmoid\": \"1/(1+exp(-x))\", \"sentinel\": \"-1e30\"}, \"validation