inputs upcast to fp32, whereas c007/c008 multiply in bf16 tensor cores. bf16 rounding shifts borderline sigmoid+bias values, flipping which group is 4th and which expert is 8th on a fraction of tokens -> wrong selected set -> positional index blowup regardless of order. Fix = make the GEMM numerically faithful. c009 (parent c007, single-variable change: GEMM precision only) upcasts the bf16 tiles to fp32 and uses tl.dot(input_precision='ieee') for a real fp32 accumulate matching the reference exactly, and restores c007's descending-by-score emit (torch.topk on CUDA returns descending). If c009 passes -> exact fp32 GEMM was the fix. If c009 still mismatches indices -> the reference order is not descending; c010 keeps exact GEMM + ascending-index emit to separate order from set.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 8, \"skills_used\": \"none\", \"next_candidate_plan\": \"c009 (parent c007): exact fp32 gate GEMM -- load bf16 tiles, .to(fp32), tl.dot(input_precision='ieee') true-fp32 accumulate (matches reference F.linear(.float())); restore c007 descending-by-score output order; single-variable change vs c007 (precision only). Then, once correct, trade precision back for speed (tf32x3/bf16) watching the 0.99 match ratio, and re-fuse / tile-tune for geomean.\"}"," {\"candidate\": \"c009\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_sha256\": \"02657b0ad88d17f9add49ade3d5aef557b60e3c51e7c855b9845e22d018540f9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T00:28:10Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"The wrong selected SET in c007/c008 came from the bf16 gate GEMM diverging from the reference's fp32 F.linear; an exact fp32 GEMM (upcast bf16 tiles to fp32, tl.dot(input_precision='ieee') true-fp32 accumulate) with c007's descending-by-score emit will match the reference set+order and pass.\", \"config\": {\"arch\": \"two-kernel split\", \"gemm\": {\"BLOCK_M\": 16, \"BLOCK_K\": 32, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1, \"precision\": \"ieee (fp32 upcast tiles, true fp32 accumulate)\"}, \"route\": {\"grid\": \"(T,)\", \"num_warps\