rence (ties are measure-zero on random data). So the selected SET is correct and the failure is purely OUTPUT ORDER: the evaluator compares topk_idx POSITIONALLY (errors ~190-249 lie in [0,255]; a dense/order-insensitive compare would bound errors by weight<=2.5, and an order-insensitive compare would make my provably-correct-set c009 PASS -- it did not, proving positional comparison). Descending-by-score order (c007,c009) does NOT match the reference positional order. Ascending-index was tried only in c008 with bf16 (set-unproven) and also failed, but precision-irrelevance means that test was not conclusive for a proven-correct set. c010 = c009's exact-fp32 kernel (provably correct set) + ascending-expert-index emit (8x8 rank + scatter, as in c008): the FIRST clean test of ascending order with a proven-correct set. If c010 passes, reference order was ascending index. If c010 also fails with ~250 max_abs, the reference uses torch.topk(sorted=False)'s native radix order (neither ascending nor descending) and I must reproduce that exact order.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 9, \"skills_used\": \"none\", \"next_candidate_plan\": \"c010 (parent c009): keep exact fp32 GEMM (provably correct selected set); change ONLY the output order to ascending expert index via the 8x8 rank + scatter store. Decisive test of order with a proven-correct set. If pass -> done (then perf-tune precision/tiling/fusion). If fail -> reproduce torch.topk(sorted=False) native order.\"}","+{\"candidate\": \"c010\", \"parent\": \"c009\", \"source_sha256\": \"249a08d53064f98e97066e36ad746aec4afb894e4fc200652bcf4a6bd90cfec2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T00:50:45Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"The reference torch.topk(masked,k=8,sorted=False) CUDA gatherTopK order is: the 7 strictly-larger experts in ASCENDING INDEX, then the kth-value (min-score selected) expert LAST. Reproducing that exact emit order on the proven-correct exact-fp32 set will pass all 5.\", \"config\": {\"arch\": \"two-kernel split\", \"gemm\": {\"BLOCK_M\": 16, \"BLOCK_K\": 32, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1, \"precision\": \"ieee fp32\"}, \"route\": {\"grid\": \"(T,)\", \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1}, \"output_order\": \"torch.topk(sorted=False): first 7 (strictly-larger) by asc index, min-score expert last (8x8 restricted rank + scatter)\", \"sigmoid\": \"1/(1+exp(-x))\", \"sentinel\": \"-1e30\"}, \"validation\": {\"static_gate_passed\": true, \"static_gate_notes\": \"exact-fp32 provably-correct set (from c009); only emit order changed vs c009; descending selection loop => pick i=TOPK-1 is the min-score/kth expert -> slot 7; picks 0..6 -> slots 0..6 by ascending expert index\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"469b2796-deb3-5a83-a7a6-1b2f84b86f20\", \"num_tokens\": 2240, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.8858762985769966, \"max_abs\": 4.76837158203125e-07, \"max_rel\": 7.266351644830138e-07}, {\"uuid\": \"993dd417-9fb2-5d66-9b81-c1e15a113463\", \"num_tokens\": 2272, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.8354636802460559, \"max_abs\": 4.917383193969727e-07, \"max_rel\": 7.565205351056647e-07}, {\"uuid\": \"0fc8f5f9-1900-55f4-b7d8-acefecbead69\", \"num_tokens\": 6144, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.9352054300402902, \"max_abs\": 5.364418029785156e-07, \"max_rel\": 8.381903171539307e-07}, {\"uuid\": \"d6d0eb83-de2e-5a6d-ba23-ee72ae216708\", \"num_tokens\": 2048, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.8020239111201585, \"max_abs\": 4.917383193969727e-07, \"max_rel\": 7.805369932611939e-07}, {\"uuid\": \"1d554a6c-1d9d-54c7-9ed9-6d4b50c95906\", \"num_tokens\": 2112, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.8434427620220671, \"max_abs\": 4.470348358154297e-07, \"max_rel\": 7.982765168890182e-07}], \"all_correct\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 0.8591917965392462, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 0.8604024164011136, \"decision\": \"champion\", \"decision_reason\": \"FIRST CORRECT CANDIDATE: 5/5 PASSED, max_abs ~5e-7 (essentially exact). The output-order hypothesis is CONFIRMED: torch.topk(sorted=False) on CUDA returns the 7 strictly-larger experts by ascending expert index followed by the min-score (kth-value) expert last. Combined with the exact-fp32 set this reproduces the reference to ulp. Geomean speedup 0.8592x -- CORRECT but SLOWER than the multi-launch reference; must now optimize. Root perf cost: (a) GEMM uses input_precision='ieee' (true fp32 dot) which on A800 is ~3-4x slower than bf16 HMMA and does NOT use the fast tensor-core path; (b) c007==c009 proved matmul precision is IRRELEVANT to the compared result for these workloads, so bf16 HMMA will still pass 5/5. Reverting the GEMM to bf16 is the single biggest, zero-correctness-risk speed lever. c011 = c010 with the GEMM reverted to bf16 (drop .to(fp32) upcast and input_precision='ieee'; keep everything else). Expect a large speedup toward/above 1.0x.\", \"cumulative_evals\": 10, \"skills_used\": \"none\", \"next_candidate_plan\": \"c011 (parent c010): revert gate GEMM to bf16 HMMA (remove the fp32 tile upcast and input_precision='ieee'; acc += tl.dot(a_bf16, b_bf16)), keeping c010's exact routing + torch.topk output order. Single-variable perf change; precision proven comparison-irrelevant (c007==c009). Then tile/tune GEMM (BLOCK_M/BLOCK_K/num_stages>=2/num_warps) and consider re-fusing the two kernels to cut the logits DRAM round-trip + second launch.\"}"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
